WEBVTT

00:00:00.698 --> 00:00:02.828
Text structure and purpose.

00:00:02.828 --> 00:00:05.138
Don't just ask what the author says.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.615
Ask what the author is doing.

00:00:08.148 --> 00:00:09.908
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:09.908 --> 00:00:14.258
The question asks for the main purpose, or the overall structure.

00:00:14.258 --> 00:00:17.135
Or it asks about one underlined sentence.

00:00:18.181 --> 00:00:21.113
It's testing the job each part of the text is doing.

00:00:22.169 --> 00:00:23.649
Here's the method.

00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:30.009
Label each sentence with a verb: introduces, describes, challenges, concludes.

00:00:30.009 --> 00:00:33.864
For purpose, combine the labels into one main action.

00:00:33.864 --> 00:00:36.964
For structure, keep the actions in order.

00:00:36.964 --> 00:00:39.509
Then check every word of the answer.

00:00:39.509 --> 00:00:41.092
One wrong verb kills it.

00:00:42.144 --> 00:00:44.089
Check the verbs carefully.

00:00:44.089 --> 00:00:46.439
Describing is not arguing.

00:00:46.439 --> 00:00:48.829
Questioning is not disproving.

00:00:48.829 --> 00:00:52.649
Function means what a sentence does, not what it says.

00:00:52.649 --> 00:00:55.789
And in two-part answers, both halves must be right.

00:00:56.826 --> 00:00:58.316
Let's try one.

00:00:58.316 --> 00:01:00.771
Label each sentence with what it does.

00:01:00.771 --> 00:01:03.901
Many people believe: that's a common belief.

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:07.961
Experiments tell a different story: that's evidence against it.

00:01:07.961 --> 00:01:10.991
Such results suggest: that's a conclusion.

00:01:10.991 --> 00:01:14.706
So the structure is belief, evidence, conclusion.

00:01:14.706 --> 00:01:17.476
Choice A says the experiment was flawed.

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:20.016
Choice C brings in other animals.

00:01:20.016 --> 00:01:22.451
Choice D argues about cruelty.

00:01:22.451 --> 00:01:24.973
Only choice B has all three, in order.

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:28.098
Watch out for the wrong verb.

00:01:28.098 --> 00:01:33.828
An answer that says argues, or criticizes, when the author only describes.

00:01:33.828 --> 00:01:36.119
One wrong word makes the whole choice wrong.

00:01:37.181 --> 00:01:44.121
Here's the whole lesson on one page: how to spot it, the four steps, the verb checks, and the trap.

00:01:44.121 --> 00:01:46.991
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
